{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-12eeab21-ef55-4c18-88f6-ab7a1940845c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The strategy is small. Let me check architecture context for Dashboard and Documentation, and see the components' context files.\n\nStep 0 triage:\n- Check 1 — below threshold: Is it S-sized? The strategy doesn't state a size. Four core flows fixed for keyboard accessibility, affecting a single component (Dashboard) for code, plus Documentation. Two teams? Dashboard and Documentation likely owned by different teams. Also multiple distinct work streams: code implementation + substantive content authoring (VPAT + accessibility statement republish — HLR-3 is substantive docs). So the escape condition \"multiple distinct work streams\" applies → proceed to Step 1.\n\nSo decomposition: \n- Implementation epic for keyboard fixes in Dashboard (HLR-1, HLR-2 — both same surface, same component; bundle).\n- docs-authoring epic for Documentation (HLR-3), blocked by the implementation (Rule 11: docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics).\n\nNo investigation (open questions: none). No external dependencies.\n\nPriorities: strategy frontmatter priority Normal → docs-authoring priority P2 (matches HLR-3 P2 anyway). Implementation epic: HLR-1 P1, HLR-2 P1 → P1.\n\nCheck architecture context for Dashboard and Documentation to score signal 9.\n\nAlso HLR-1 and HLR-2 — same component, same team, same surface (audited flows) → single epic.\n\nLet me look at .context/architecture-context/.","signature":"fd464740f2244f89afe728a922a2fa61"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18680,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94260a1e048cfd9","agent_id":"a33d498ebb9da0ed9","session_id":"78ea6462-0cc2-4c3f-86ff-bd63945000c9","uuid":"2744f278-0a8f-4dd9-9433-7c181564ed70","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:13:43.475Z","subagent_type":"c