{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0b7d1fe0-7558-43dc-bb51-9c04403f073b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bbf30b4f3997421","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-2aud1zj5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md","content":"# Keyboard accessibility fixes for core Dashboard flows\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the accessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion, all four flows are fully operable with keyboard alone — no focus traps, no unreachable controls — and visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows. This is the code deliverable that the updated conformance documentation will describe.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Fix each keyboard accessibility defect enumerated in the audit report for the four audited core flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission):\n  - Restore and manage focus correctly in modals (focus moved into the modal on open, trapped while open, returned to the invoking control on close).\n  - Make every control in the audited flows reachable and operable via keyboard (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the pattern requires it, keyboard-activatable actions).\n  - Apply the consistent visible focus indicator treatment across the audited flows so the indicator is uniform rather than varying per control or per page.\n- Cover both keyboard operability (no focus traps, no unreachable controls) and focus-indicator consistency in the same pass over the same UI surfaces.\n- Verify no regression to pointer-based interaction in the audited flows.\n- Out of scope (per strategy): screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones. Incidental reference updates that fall out of these fixes (e.g. a changed control label referenced in nearby docs) are folded in here rather than split out.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited core flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed start-to-finish using the keyboard alone.\n- No focus traps exist in the audited flows: focus is managed into, within, and out of modals without keyboard users becoming stuck.\n- No control in the audited flows is unreachable or inoperable via keyboard; every defect enumerated in the audit report for these flows is resolved or explicitly dispositioned with rationale.\n- Visible focus indicators are consistent (uniform style and visibility) across all controls in the audited flows.\n- Pointer-based interaction in the audited flows continues to work as before (no regressions).\n- The Dashboard build pipeline (CI) is green with the changes included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls. Core scope of this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows. Consolidated with HLR-1 in this epic: both requirements edit the same UI surfaces in the same four flows, so a split would double-touch the same components.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24478,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a94260a1e048cfd9","agent_id":"a33d498ebb9da0ed9","session_id":"78ea6462-0cc2-4c3f-86ff-bd63945000c9","uuid":"0f191f39-67c9-46cf-aa08-1f22c9e7a896","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:14:58.734Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
