{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9535610d8ae73c20","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility fixes for core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility fixes for core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the accessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion, all four flows are fully operable with keyboard alone — no focus traps, no unreachable controls — and visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows. This is the code deliverable that the updated conformance documentation will describe.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Fix each keyboard accessibility defect enumerated in the audit report for the four audited core flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission):\n38\t  - Restore and manage focus correctly in modals (focus moved into the modal on open, trapped while open, returned to the invoking control on close).\n39\t  - Make every control in the audited flows reachable and operable via keyboard (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the pattern requires it, keyboard-activatable actions).\n40\t  - Apply the consistent visible focus indicator treatment across the audited flows so the indicator is uniform rather than varying per control or per page.\n41\t- Cover both keyboard operability (no focus traps, no unreachable controls) and focus-indicator consistency in the same pass over the same UI surfaces.\n42\t- Verify no regression to pointer-based interaction in the audited flows.\n43\t- Out of scope (per strategy): screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones. Incidental reference updates that fall out of these fixes (e.g. a changed control label referenced in nearby docs) are folded in here rather than split out.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Each of the four audited core flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed start-to-finish using the keyboard alone.\n48\t- No focus traps exist in the audited flows: focus is managed into, within, and out of modals without keyboard users becoming stuck.\n49\t- No control in the audited flows is unreachable or inoperable via keyboard; every defect enumerated in the audit report for these flows is resolved or explicitly dispositioned with rationale.\n50\t- Visible focus indicators are consistent (uniform style and visibility) across all controls in the audited flows.\n51\t- Pointer-based interaction in the audited flows continues to work as before (no regressions).\n52\t- The Dashboard build pipeline (CI) is green with the changes included.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls. Core scope of this epic.\n57\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows. Consolidated with HLR-1 in this epic: both requirements edit the same UI surfaces in the same four flows, so a split would double-touch the same components.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acd9037abe4491d8","agent_id":"a84597708584e0709","session_id":"78ea6462-0cc2-4c3f-86ff-bd63945000c9","uuid":"b527e8b3-5c3b-4e8b-8753-fb072c878906","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:16:53.009Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9535610d8ae73c20","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
