{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14a9ebd45075774","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\tContract validator: OK (exit 0, no violations). Triage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 2 epics — no triage contradiction. No conditional branch files exist, and none are required (no bounded-outcome decisions in the strategy).\n15\t\n16\t## Criterion Details\n17\t\n18\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n19\tAll three HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P1) → E001, HLR-3 (P2) → E002. The HLR Traceability Matrix is present in the summary and each epic has an HLR Traceability section. Priority handling is correct: E001 takes P1 (highest of its HLRs); E002 is a `docs-authoring` epic, exempt from priority inheritance, and its P2 correctly derives from the strategy's `priority: Normal` while also matching HLR-3's P2 label. No priority collapse: HLR-1/HLR-2 are both P1 over the same four UI surfaces (consolidation is correct, not collapse), and the P2 documentation work is in its own independently plannable epic. The consolidation rationale for HLR-1+HLR-2 (same component, team, and surfaces; a split would double-touch the same code) is recorded in the matrix.\n20\t\n21\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n22\tSingle edge E001 → E002, correctly justified by Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics). Cross-check passes: the diagram (`graph TD`, dependency → dependent) matches frontmatter exactly — E001 `dependencies: []`, E002 `dependencies: [RHAISTRAT-9017-E001]`. No circular or invalid edges. No `konflux-onboarding`, `repo-onboarding`, or `license-validation` epics exist, so the Rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints do not apply. Critical path length 2 is appropriate for a small strategy (S: 1-2)